Flag<code>argon:power_tag_parents</code> <p>Palladium's <code>depends_on</code> ties a power to one specific parent power. With this flag, a power can instead name a tag of powers, and a player can get the power while they hold any power in that tag.</p> <p>Two settings are added to the power file (<code>data/&lt;namespace&gt;/palladium/power/&lt;name&gt;.json</code>).</p> Key Type Description Required Fallback <code>parent_tag</code> Power tag The tag of powers that count as a parent, for example <code>palladium:main_power</code>. A power without this key behaves as it does in Palladium. No None <code>parent_required</code> Boolean When <code>true</code>, the player must hold a power in <code>parent_tag</code>. When <code>false</code>, the power can be added whether or not they do. No <code>true</code> <p>A power that already uses Palladium's <code>depends_on</code> keeps that behavior and ignores these settings.</p> <pre><code>{
  "name": {
    "translate": "power.example.herald.name"
  },
  "parent_tag": "palladium:main_power",
  "parent_required": false
}
</code></pre> <p>Without the flag, both keys are ignored and powers use Palladium's normal rules.</p>

ID<code>argon:ability_bar</code> Holds the data for an ability bar widget. Players fill its slots from an ability pool, with optional presets and crouch variants. Does nothing on its own. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>abilities</code>StringList of ability pool entries the player can choose from for each slot.✓/<code>slots</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many ability bar slots to offer.✗5<code>presets</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many switchable sets of slot assignments to offer, where 1 disables the preset-switching arrows.✗1<code>crouch_variants</code>BooleanWhether each slot also accepts a separate, crouch-only ability assignment.✗false<code>hide_unavailable</code>BooleanHides pool abilities the player can't get yet in the slot picker. Ignores ability_bar_active checks when deciding that.✗true</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:ability_bar",
  "abilities": [
    "argon:example#ability_1",
    "argon:example#ability_2"
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:ability_bar",
  "abilities": [
    {
      "ability": "argon:example#ability_1",
      "slot": 0
    },
    {
      "ability": "argon:example#ability_2",
      "list_index_slot": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": 3,
  "crouch_variants": true
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "ability_bar": {
      "type": "argon:ability_bar",
      "abilities": [
        "argon:example#ability_1",
        "argon:example#ability_2"
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:ability_data_attachment_modifier</code> While enabled, watches a list of other abilities. For each enabled one it adds to, subtracts from or sets a shared number data attachment, at its own rate and timer. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>attachment</code>Data Attachment IDThe id of the number-valued data attachment to modify, shared by every entry.✓/<code>abilities</code>Attachment Modifier,Attachment Modifier[]Each entry references one of the entity's own abilities (e.g. "fsang:marvel/mutant/cosmic_herald#some_ability"), an operation* ("add" default, "subtract", or "set"), a value used by that operation, and a rate* (default 20 ticks) - the referenced ability's own enabled state is checked every tick, and the modification fires every "rate" ticks it stays enabled.✓/</p> <p><p><code>abilities</code> (Attachment Modifier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>ability</code>Ability ReferenceThe ability whose value is changed.✓/<code>operation</code><code>add</code><code>subtract</code><code>set</code>How the value is applied.✗/<code>value</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe amount to add, subtract or set.✓/<code>rate</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How often the change is applied.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:ability_data_attachment_modifier",
  "attachment": "example:my_attachment",
  "abilities": [
    {
      "ability": "example:my_power#some_ability",
      "value": 1
    },
    {
      "ability": "example:my_power#other_ability",
      "operation": "subtract",
      "value": 2,
      "rate": 40
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "ability_data_attachment_modifier": {
      "type": "argon:ability_data_attachment_modifier",
      "attachment": "example:my_attachment",
      "abilities": [
        {
          "ability": "example:my_power#some_ability",
          "value": 1
        },
        {
          "ability": "example:my_power#other_ability",
          "operation": "subtract",
          "value": 2,
          "rate": 40
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:anchored_beam</code> While enabled, draws the beam_renderer from a body part, "length" blocks long. Visual only, no aiming or damage. With an animation_timer the beam grows and shrinks. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>beam_renderer</code>IdentifierThe id of the beam renderer whose segments to render in place.✓/<code>length</code>FloatHow far, in blocks, each segment reaches past its body_part/offset anchor, in the same direction.✗0.5<code>rotation</code>Vector 3DEuler rotation in degrees (applied X then Y then Z) that tilts which way each segment extends, relative to its own body part's local space - independent of the offset's own direction. E.g. [90, 0, 0] to swing a segment that otherwise hangs straight down (the default with no offset) so it points forward instead, like an upright held tool.✗( 0.000E+0  0.000E+0  0.000E+0)<code>yaw_only</code>BooleanIf true, the beam only turns with the body's facing and ignores lean, pitch and roll, so it stays level. The start point still follows the body part.✗false</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:anchored_beam",
  "beam_renderer": "example:beam_renderer_id",
  "rotation": [
    90,
    0,
    0
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "anchored_beam": {
      "type": "argon:anchored_beam",
      "beam_renderer": "example:beam_renderer_id",
      "rotation": [
        90,
        0,
        0
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:area_burst</code> On its first enabled tick, hits every living entity in a sphere or cone around the user once with damage, armor penetration, knockback and effects. Can deflect or destroy projectiles. Skips the user, pets, teammates and armor stands. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>sphere</code><code>cone</code>"sphere" hits everything within the radius. "cone" only hits what is inside cone_angle of where the user looks.✗sphere<code>radius</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far the burst reaches, in blocks.✓/<code>cone_angle</code>FloatThe full opening angle of the cone, in degrees.✗60.0<code>damage</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe damage dealt to each entity hit.✗/<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDThe damage type used; the user's normal attack when left out.✗/<code>armor_penetration</code>FloatThe fraction from 0 to 1 of a hit entity's armor that is ignored.✗0.0<code>falloff</code>FloatFrom 0 to 1, how much damage and knockback are reduced for entities at the very edge of the burst.✗0.0<code>knockback_distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far, in blocks, hit entities are pushed away from the user. Weakened by knockback resistance.✗/<code>lift</code>(Dynamic) ValueUpward launch speed added to the knockback.✗/<code>movement_limit</code>Movement LimitScales knockback and lift down for wide entities, as on energy beams.✗/<code>effects</code>Beam Effect[]Mob effects applied to every entity hit.✗/<code>projectiles</code><code>none</code><code>deflect</code><code>destroy</code>"deflect" sends projectiles in range away from the user. "destroy" removes them. The user's own projectiles are left alone.✗none<code>hostile_only</code>BooleanIf true, only hostile mobs are affected.✗false<code>dispel</code>DispelRemoves up to count effects of the given category ("beneficial" or "harmful") from every entity hit, longest first. Bosses are skipped unless skip_bosses is false.✗/<code>look_target_range</code>DoubleIf set, the burst is centered where the user looks, up to this many blocks away, instead of on the user.✗/<code>push</code><code>radial</code><code>path_side</code>"radial" pushes hit entities straight away from the user. "path_side" pushes them sideways, off the line the user is travelling along, towards the side they are already on.✗radial<code>visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle visuals spawned at the centre of the burst, in the same format as the visuals of argon:energy_beam, for example a ring.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>movement_limit</code> (Movement Limit)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>full_below_width</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)Targets up to this wide, in blocks, are pushed with full strength.✗1.0<code>none_above_width</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)Targets at least this wide, in blocks, are not pushed at all. In between, the push fades out.✗3.0<code>immovable</code>Entity Type TagEntities in this tag are never pushed.✗/</p> <p><p><code>effects[]</code> (Beam Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)The effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/<code>size_tiers</code>Size Tier[]Changes or skips the effect depending on the width or type of the target.✗/</p> <p><p><code>effects[].size_tiers[]</code> (Size Tier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>tag</code>Entity Type TagOnly entities in this tag use the tier.✗/<code>min_width</code>Double (0.0 ~ 64.0)The tier applies to entities at least this wide, in blocks.✗0.0<code>skip</code>BooleanIf true, matching entities do not get the effect at all.✗false<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDReplaces the effect for matching entities.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)Replaces the amplifier for matching entities.✗/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Replaces the duration for matching entities.✗/</p> <p><p><code>dispel</code> (Dispel)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>category</code><code>beneficial</code><code>harmful</code>Which category of effects is removed.✗/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 64)How many effects are removed at most.✗/<code>skip_bosses</code>BooleanIf true, boss mobs are not dispelled.✗/</p> <p><p><code>visuals[]</code> (Beam Visual)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>streak</code><code>helix</code><code>ring</code><code>sphere</code><code>burst</code><code>crescent</code>The particle pattern to draw.✓/<code>anchor</code><code>end</code><code>caster</code>Whether the pattern is drawn at the end of the beam or around the caster.✗/<code>orientation</code><code>horizontal</code><code>vertical</code>How ring and crescent patterns are turned.✗/<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle used.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 512)How many particles the pattern uses.✗/<code>radius</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The radius of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>step</code>Float (0.05 ~ 16.0)The spacing between particles along the beam.✗/<code>pitch</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The length of one full twist for helixes, in blocks.✗/<code>strands</code>Integer (1 ~ 8)How many strands a helix has.✗/<code>arc</code>Float (1.0 ~ 360.0)How much of a circle is drawn, in degrees.✗/<code>height</code>FloatThe height of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>rings</code>Integer (1 ~ 16)How many rings are drawn.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>spread</code>Float (0.0 ~ 8.0)How far the particles scatter.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:area_burst",
  "radius": 6,
  "damage": 8
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "area_burst": {
      "type": "argon:area_burst",
      "radius": 6,
      "damage": 8
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:restore_equipment</code> Puts items stored under an ID by the store_equipment ability back into their original slots, then forgets that ID. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>id</code>StringThe ID to restore, matching the one used by the store_equipment ability that stored them.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:restore_equipment",
  "id": "civilian_clothes"
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "restore_equipment": {
      "type": "argon:restore_equipment",
      "id": "civilian_clothes"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:store_equipment</code> Stores the items in the given slots under an ID and empties those slots. A matching restore_equipment ability puts them back later. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>id</code>StringThe ID the stored items are saved under.✓/<code>slots</code><code>mainhand</code><code>offhand</code><code>head</code><code>chest</code><code>legs</code><code>feet</code><code>body</code><code>curios:head</code><code>curios:necklace</code>The slots whose items should be stored and cleared.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:store_equipment",
  "id": "civilian_clothes",
  "slots": [
    "head",
    "chest",
    "legs",
    "feet"
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "store_equipment": {
      "type": "argon:store_equipment",
      "id": "civilian_clothes",
      "slots": [
        "head",
        "chest",
        "legs",
        "feet"
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:auto_attack</code> While enabled, walks toward the nearest mob in range, jumping over obstacles, and hits it with the held item once it is close enough. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>DoubleHow far from the player a mob can be to be selected as a target and chased.✓/<code>attack_range</code>DoubleHow close the target needs to be before the player stops moving and attacks it instead.✓/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe player's movement speed, in blocks per tick, while chasing a target outside attack range.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:auto_attack",
  "range": 8,
  "attack_range": 2.5,
  "speed": 0.3
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "auto_attack": {
      "type": "argon:auto_attack",
      "range": 8,
      "attack_range": 2.5,
      "speed": 0.3
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:biome_swap</code> While enabled, replaces the terrain within "radius" of where it started with fresh "biome" terrain (optionally in a black concrete shell). Every changed block is restored on disable. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>radius</code>DoubleHow far from the entity's position (1-64) the swap reaches.✓/<code>biome</code>IdentifierThe biome(s) to generate, vanilla or modded. A single ID, a list of IDs, or a list that mixes IDs with objects that also give a status effect to entities in the area (see the second example).✓/<code>height_below</code>IntegerHow many blocks below the entity's feet are included when sphere is false.✗4<code>height_above</code>IntegerHow many blocks above the entity's feet are included when sphere is false.✗4<code>sphere</code>BooleanIf true, the area is a full sphere inside a solid black concrete shell instead of a column limited by radius.✗false<code>unbreakable</code>BooleanIf true, none of the newly added blocks can be broken while the ability is enabled.✗true<code>build_animation</code>BooleanIf true, the area grows in and shrinks out over a couple of seconds instead of popping in and out.✗true</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:biome_swap",
  "radius": 10,
  "biome": "minecraft:desert"
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:biome_swap",
  "radius": 16,
  "biome": [
    {
      "biome": "minecraft:crimson_forest",
      "effect": "minecraft:fire_resistance",
      "amplifier": 1,
      "affect_self": false
    },
    "minecraft:deep_dark"
  ],
  "height_below": 6,
  "height_above": 8,
  "sphere": true,
  "unbreakable": false,
  "build_animation": false
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "biome_swap": {
      "type": "argon:biome_swap",
      "radius": 10,
      "biome": "minecraft:desert"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:blast_chain</code> Fires a beam that only damages on reaching its target. If it hits a living entity it fires on to the nearest other visible living entity, up to "chain_count" more times. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>beam_renderer</code>IdentifierThe id of the beam renderer to use for every segment of the chain.✓/<code>damage</code>FloatThe damage dealt to the entity hit by the initial shot.✗0.0<code>damage_falloff</code>FloatMultiplier on "damage" for each jump already taken (0.85 means the 2nd hit deals 85%, the 3rd 72.25%). 1 means no falloff. Effects keep their full strength.✗1.0<code>max_distance</code>FloatThe maximum distance the initial shot can travel before giving up.✗30.0<code>speed</code>FloatThe blocks every beam piece (initial shot and every chain jump) travels per tick.✗2.0<code>length</code>FloatThe length of the traveling beam piece, in blocks.✗4.0<code>set_on_fire_ticks</code>IntegerHow many ticks each hit entity is set on fire for.✗0<code>cause_fire</code>BooleanIf the initial shot should ignite flammable blocks it hits instead of a living entity.✗false<code>smelt_blocks</code>BooleanIf the initial shot should smelt the block it hits instead of a living entity.✗false<code>chain_count</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)The maximum number of additional jumps after the initial hit.✗3<code>chain_range</code>FloatHow far, in blocks, from each impact point to search for the next chain target.✗8.0<code>can_hit_caster</code>BooleanWhether a jump can pick the caster as its next target. The first shot never hits the caster.✗false<code>effects</code>Potion Hit Effect,Potion Hit Effect[]Applied, at full configured strength, to every entity hit by the chain (the initial hit and every jump). Same entry format as "potion_hit"'s "effects": effect, duration, amplifier, max_amplifier and particles*.✗[]<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDA damage type ID such as "minecraft:magic" or one from a pack. Left unset, it is a player attack when a player uses this and a mob attack otherwise. Unknown types fall back to that.✗/</p> <p><p><code>effects</code> (Potion Hit Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✓/<code>amplifier</code>IntegerThe effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>max_amplifier</code>IntegerThe highest level repeated hits can stack the effect up to.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:blast_chain",
  "beam_renderer": "example:beam_renderer_id",
  "damage": 6,
  "damage_falloff": 0.85,
  "max_distance": 25,
  "speed": 2.5,
  "effects": {
    "effect": "minecraft:poison",
    "duration": 60,
    "max_amplifier": 3
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "blast_chain": {
      "type": "argon:blast_chain",
      "beam_renderer": "example:beam_renderer_id",
      "damage": 6,
      "damage_falloff": 0.85,
      "max_distance": 25,
      "speed": 2.5,
      "effects": {
        "effect": "minecraft:poison",
        "duration": 60,
        "max_amplifier": 3
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:blink</code> On activation, teleports you up to "distance" blocks along your look direction. Stops before solid blocks, and can pass through see-through ones like glass ("allow_see_through"). SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe maximum distance, in blocks, the user is teleported.✓/<code>allow_see_through</code>BooleanWhether see-through solid blocks (glass etc.) are passed through instead of stopping the teleport.✗true<code>safe</code>BooleanIf true, the blink fails (nothing happens) when the destination is inside blocks, in or over lava, fire or magma, cactus, or over the void.✗false<code>respect_protection</code>BooleanIf true, the blink fails when a player user could not interact with the destination blocks (spawn protection, claim mods).✗false<code>particles</code>Particle Effect[]Optional particle effects played at the user's start and end positions in list order, skipped if the user doesn't actually move, where each entry is a full particle options object with an optional world-space offset.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>particles[]</code> (Particle Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle to spawn.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)How many particles spawn.✗/<code>spread</code>DoubleHow far the particles spread from the origin.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>offset</code>Vector 3DOffset from the origin in blocks.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:blink",
  "distance": 20,
  "properties": {
    "title": "Blink"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:blink",
  "distance": 10,
  "allow_see_through": false,
  "particles": [
    {
      "particle": {
        "type": "minecraft:portal"
      },
      "count": 30
    },
    {
      "particle": {
        "type": "minecraft:cloud"
      },
      "count": 30,
      "offset": [
        0,
        1,
        0
      ]
    }
  ],
  "properties": {
    "title": "Blink"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "blink": {
      "type": "argon:blink",
      "distance": 20,
      "properties": {
        "title": "Blink"
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:block_energy</code> While enabled, drains RF from or adds RF to the block you look at, every tick, as long as it is within range and exposes an energy storage. With an energy_bar the drained RF fills that bar and added RF is taken from it, otherwise the RF is simply removed from or created in the block. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>mode</code>String"drain" pulls RF out of the block, "add" pushes RF into it, "toggle" adds while the user is sneaking and drains otherwise.✗drain<code>range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far away, in blocks, the block can be.✗8<code>rate</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe most RF moved per tick.✗100<code>energy_bar</code>StringAn energy bar, as "power#bar_name". Drained RF fills it and added RF is spent from it. Left unset, no bar is used and the energy is unlimited.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:block_energy",
  "mode": "drain",
  "range": 8,
  "rate": 200,
  "energy_bar": "example:power#energy"
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "block_energy": {
      "type": "argon:block_energy",
      "mode": "drain",
      "range": 8,
      "rate": 200,
      "energy_bar": "example:power#energy"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:block_scan</code> While enabled, shows a panel next to the crosshair for the block you look at: active or powered, energy, fluids, items, connections, damage and readable text. Only what the game exposes is shown. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far away, in blocks, a block can be read from.✗8<code>blocks</code>Block ID(s) / TagLimit the scan to these blocks, given as explicit block IDs, a tag ("#namespace:tag"), or a mix of both. Left unset, any block that has something to read is scanned.✗/<code>show_status</code>BooleanShow whether the block is active (lit / enabled / powered) and the redstone signal it receives.✗true<code>show_energy</code>BooleanShow stored energy and capacity.✗true<code>show_fluids</code>BooleanShow the fluids stored in the block's tanks.✗true<code>show_items</code>BooleanShow how full the block's inventory is and the main items in it.✗true<code>show_connections</code>BooleanShow which neighbouring blocks it connects to (they have energy, fluid or item storage facing it).✗true<code>show_damage</code>BooleanShow damage the block's state reports (chipped / damaged anvils, cracked blocks).✗true<code>show_info</code>BooleanShow readable information the block carries (a sign's text, a command block's command).✗true</p> <pre><code>{
