ID<code>argon:collision_attack</code> While enabled and moving faster than "min_speed", every living entity the user runs into takes damage and is knocked away along the user's direction of travel. Damage and knockback grow with how far the speed is above "min_speed". Each target can only be hit again after "hit_cooldown" ticks. Allied entities, the user's vehicle and passengers are skipped. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>min_speed</code>DoubleHorizontal speed in blocks per second the user has to exceed before anything is hit.✗20.0<code>damage</code>DoubleDamage dealt at exactly min_speed.✗4.0<code>damage_per_speed</code>DoubleExtra damage for every block per second above min_speed.✗0.25<code>knockback</code>DoubleKnockback strength at exactly min_speed.✗0.8<code>knockback_per_speed</code>DoubleExtra knockback strength for every block per second above min_speed.✗0.03<code>upward_knockback</code>DoubleUpward velocity added to the target when it is hit.✗0.3<code>inflation</code>DoubleHow much the user's hitbox is grown, in blocks, when looking for entities to hit. The box is also stretched along the distance moved this tick so fast runs cannot skip over targets.✗0.4<code>hit_cooldown</code>IntegerTicks before the same target can be hit again.✗20<code>affect_players</code>BooleanIf false, other players are never hit.✗true<code>excluded_entities</code>Identifier[]Entity types that are never hit, so the run passes straight through them. Defaults to minecraft:armor_stand and palladium:suit_stand.✗/<code>hit_effects</code>Potion Hit Effect,Potion Hit Effect[]Effects applied to every target that is hit, for example bleeding.✗[]<code>effects_min_speed</code>DoubleHorizontal speed in blocks per second the user has to reach before hit_effects, hit_visuals and hit_sound are used. Slower hits only do damage.✗0.0<code>hit_visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle visuals spawned at every target that is hit, in the same format as the visuals of argon:energy_beam.✗[]<code>visuals_require_blood</code>BooleanIf true, hit_visuals are skipped for entities in the argon:bloodless tag, so blood particles do not appear on things that cannot bleed.✗false<code>hit_sound</code>IdentifierA sound event played at every target that is hit, instead of the default hit sound.✗/<code>hit_sound_volume</code>FloatVolume of hit_sound.✗1.0<code>hit_sound_pitch</code>FloatPitch of hit_sound.✗0.9</p> <p><p><code>hit_effects</code> (Potion Hit Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✓/<code>amplifier</code>IntegerThe effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>max_amplifier</code>IntegerThe highest level repeated hits can stack the effect up to.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/</p> <p><p><code>hit_visuals[]</code> (Beam Visual)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>streak</code><code>helix</code><code>ring</code><code>sphere</code><code>burst</code><code>crescent</code>The particle pattern to draw.✓/<code>anchor</code><code>end</code><code>caster</code>Whether the pattern is drawn at the end of the beam or around the caster.✗/<code>orientation</code><code>horizontal</code><code>vertical</code>How ring and crescent patterns are turned.✗/<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle used.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 512)How many particles the pattern uses.✗/<code>radius</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The radius of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>step</code>Float (0.05 ~ 16.0)The spacing between particles along the beam.✗/<code>pitch</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The length of one full twist for helixes, in blocks.✗/<code>strands</code>Integer (1 ~ 8)How many strands a helix has.✗/<code>arc</code>Float (1.0 ~ 360.0)How much of a circle is drawn, in degrees.✗/<code>height</code>FloatThe height of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>rings</code>Integer (1 ~ 16)How many rings are drawn.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>spread</code>Float (0.0 ~ 8.0)How far the particles scatter.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:collision_attack",
  "properties": {
    "title": "Collision Attack"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
