ID<code>argon:color_cycle_glow</code> While enabled, gives the entity an outline that cycles through "colors" in order. It follows world time so everyone sees the same color. Independent of entity_glow and the Glowing effect. By default it is visible through walls, and the outline is a solid colour, so "intensity" dims it towards black. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>colors</code>Color[]The ordered list of colors to cycle through and fade between; must contain at least one color.✓/<code>rate</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many ticks (20 per second) each fade from one color to the next takes.✗20<code>intensity</code>Float / Value(Dynamic) 0 to 1, how strong the outline is. The outline is always opaque, so this mixes the colour from faded_color (at 0) to the cycling colour (at 1), for example from an argon:power_age value.✗1.0<code>faded_color</code>ColorThe colour the outline mixes towards as intensity drops to 0, black by default.✗#000000<code>through_walls</code>BooleanIf false, the outline is only shown to viewers who have a clear line of sight to the entity, so it disappears behind blocks.✗true</p> <pre><code>{
