ID<code>argon:damage_reaction</code> While enabled, the first reaction matching an incoming hit changes it. It can scale or cancel damage, cancel knockback, hit the attacker back, give effects, and cut another ability's cooldown. argon:reacted can check the last reaction. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>reactions</code>Damage Reaction[]Checked in order, the first match wins. kind is "any", "melee" or "projectile"; min_damage is the smallest hit it applies to; damage_multiplier is how much of the damage still goes through (0 cancels the hit); counter_damage is a Value dealt back to a living attacker; attacker_effects and self_effects are lists of { effect, duration, amplifier, particles }; cooldown_cap is { ability, cap* } and lowers that key bind ability's remaining cooldown to at most cap.✓/</p> <p><p><code>reactions[]</code> (Damage Reaction)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>id</code>StringA name for the reaction.✗/<code>kind</code><code>any</code><code>melee</code><code>projectile</code>Which kind of damage triggers the reaction.✗/<code>min_damage</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)The damage has to be at least this much.✗0.0<code>damage_multiplier</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)Multiplies the damage taken.✗/<code>cancel_knockback</code>BooleanWhether the knockback is cancelled.✗/<code>counter_damage</code>(Dynamic) ValueDamage dealt back to the attacker.✗/<code>attacker_effects</code>Beam Effect[]Effects applied to the attacker.✗/<code>self_effects</code>Beam Effect[]Effects applied to the user.✗/<code>cooldown_cap</code>Cooldown CapCuts down the cooldown of another ability.✗/</p> <p><p><code>reactions[].attacker_effects[]</code> (Beam Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)The effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/<code>size_tiers</code>Size Tier[]Changes or skips the effect depending on the width or type of the target.✗/</p> <p><p><code>reactions[].attacker_effects[].size_tiers[]</code> (Size Tier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>tag</code>Entity Type TagOnly entities in this tag use the tier.✗/<code>min_width</code>Double (0.0 ~ 64.0)The tier applies to entities at least this wide, in blocks.✗0.0<code>skip</code>BooleanIf true, matching entities do not get the effect at all.✗false<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDReplaces the effect for matching entities.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)Replaces the amplifier for matching entities.✗/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Replaces the duration for matching entities.✗/</p> <p><p><code>reactions[].cooldown_cap</code> (Cooldown Cap)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>ability</code>Ability ReferenceThe ability whose cooldown is capped.✓/<code>cap</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The cooldown is cut down to at most this long.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:damage_reaction",
  "reactions": []
}
