ID<code>argon:danger_sense</code> While enabled, detects hostile mobs (and neutral ones targeting you) within "hostile_range" and players who recently damaged you. Can light the screen border toward each danger. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>hostile_range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far to search for hostile mobs, checked fresh every scan. Also the glow's fade-in distance. A danger's glow eases from invisible at this range to full strength as it gets closer.✓/<code>attacker_memory_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long after being damaged a player who dealt that damage still counts as a detected danger.✓/<code>blacklist_powers</code>Power ID[]Entities holding any of these powers never trigger danger sense, whether they're a nearby hostile mob or a recent attacker.✗[]<code>show_visual</code>BooleanIf true, lights up the screen's border in the direction of each detected danger.✗false<code>glow_color</code>ColorThe color of the screen-border glow, when "show_visual" is true.✗#FF3333<code>glow_opacity</code>FloatThe glow's peak opacity at its brightest point, from 0 (invisible) to 1 (fully opaque).✗0.6<code>glow_thickness</code>FloatHow far the glow reaches inward from the screen's edge, in pixels.✗28.0<code>glow_spread</code>FloatHow far, in pixels along the screen border, the glow spreads from its brightest point before fading out.✗220.0<code>warn_projectiles</code>BooleanIf true, projectiles flying toward the holder (arrows, fireballs, tridents and the like, never the holder's own) count as dangers too and light the screen border like a mob would. Needs "show_visual" to be seen.✗false<code>projectile_range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far to look for incoming projectiles when "warn_projectiles" is on.✗24.0</p> <pre><code>{
