ID<code>argon:dodge</code> On activation, launches the entity sideways toward its WASD input, or straight backward if no movement key is held. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>velocity_modifier</code>FloatThe multiplier applied to the dodge direction when this ability activates.✓/<code>animation_ticks</code>IntegerHow many ticks the dodge pose is held after activating, for animation purposes.✗6<code>flying_velocity_modifier</code>FloatThe multiplier used instead of velocity_modifier while flying. Unset, it matches velocity_modifier.✗/<code>flying_follow_look</code>BooleanWhether a dodge while flying follows where the entity looks, including up and down, so it can be used to maneuver in the air. Otherwise it stays horizontal.✗true<code>ticks</code>IntegerIf above 1, the dodge is a sustained burst: for this many ticks the sideways speed is set to velocity_modifier blocks per tick towards the chosen direction, so it covers about ticks times velocity_modifier blocks on the ground or in the air. It stops early on hitting a wall and afterwards the entity keeps its earlier speed. Not used while flying.✗1<code>idle_forward</code>BooleanIf true, the direction used when no movement key is held is straight forward instead of backward.✗false<code>visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle visuals spawned around the entity when the dodge starts, in the same format as the visuals of argon:energy_beam. Use anchor caster to centre a ring on the user.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>visuals[]</code> (Beam Visual)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>streak</code><code>helix</code><code>ring</code><code>sphere</code><code>burst</code><code>crescent</code>The particle pattern to draw.✓/<code>anchor</code><code>end</code><code>caster</code>Whether the pattern is drawn at the end of the beam or around the caster.✗/<code>orientation</code><code>horizontal</code><code>vertical</code>How ring and crescent patterns are turned.✗/<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle used.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 512)How many particles the pattern uses.✗/<code>radius</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The radius of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>step</code>Float (0.05 ~ 16.0)The spacing between particles along the beam.✗/<code>pitch</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The length of one full twist for helixes, in blocks.✗/<code>strands</code>Integer (1 ~ 8)How many strands a helix has.✗/<code>arc</code>Float (1.0 ~ 360.0)How much of a circle is drawn, in degrees.✗/<code>height</code>FloatThe height of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>rings</code>Integer (1 ~ 16)How many rings are drawn.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>spread</code>Float (0.0 ~ 8.0)How far the particles scatter.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
