ID<code>argon:energy_beam</code> Shoots a beam that can bounce off blocks. On hitting a matching entity it can redirect onward or spread into several beams once. Applies damage, fire and smelting along its path. SettingsExample 1Example 2Example 3Example 4Example 5In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>beam_renderer</code>IdentifierThe id of the beam renderer to use.✓/<code>damage</code>(Dynamic) ValueDamage dealt to every entity the beam hits. A value, so it can follow a data attachment to scale with a level.✗0<code>max_distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueTotal distance the beam can travel across all its bounces. A value, so it can follow a data attachment to scale with a level.✗30<code>max_bounces</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)Most times the beam can bounce off blocks or entities (a spread counts as one) before stopping at its next hit.✗4<code>set_on_fire_ticks</code>IntegerHow many ticks the beam sets a hit entity on fire for.✗0<code>cause_fire</code>BooleanWhether the beam ignites flammable blocks it touches.✗false<code>smelt_blocks</code>BooleanWhether the beam smelts every block it touches.✗false<code>redirect_off_blocks</code>BooleanWhether the beam bounces off blocks instead of stopping at them. When false, only 'entity_reaction' can redirect it.✗true<code>entity_reaction</code><code>none</code><code>redirect</code><code>spread</code>What happens when the beam hits an entity matching 'entity_bounce_condition': continue, redirect, or spread into multiple beams.✗NONE<code>entity_bounce_condition</code>Condition,Condition[]A condition limiting which hit entities can redirect or spread the beam. Ignored when 'entity_reaction' is 'none', otherwise defaults to all entities.✗/<code>spread_count</code>Integer (&gt; 0)Number of beams the spread effect bursts into when 'entity_reaction' is 'spread'.✗5<code>spread_angle</code>FloatAngle in degrees the spread beams fan out from the central reflected direction when 'entity_reaction' is 'spread'.✗25.0<code>cone</code>ConeMakes damage, fire, smelting and block mode reach across a cone instead of a line. Widths in blocks at the eyes ("start_size", 0.1) and at "end_distance" (default "max_distance"); "rays" (1-128, default 24) finds blocks. Pair with the argon:cone renderer.✗/<code>knockback</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow hard the beam pushes living entities away from the caster. 1 is firm, 5 is a gale, 0 is none. Knockback resistance weakens it. A value, so it can follow a data attachment to scale with a level.✗0<code>knockback_ignores_resistance</code>BooleanWhether "knockback" ignores the target's knockback resistance.✗false<code>block_mode</code>Block ModeWhat the beam does to blocks it hits: "type" is "melt" or "freeze", with "time" (default 60 ticks), "auto_time", "speed_multiplier", "modifiers", "conversions" and "particle"; freeze adds "frozen_time", "slippery", "friction" and "snow_layers". See the examples.✗/<code>charge</code>Beam ChargeTurns the beam into a charged shot: hold the ability to charge and release to fire. Releasing before "min_time" (default 10) fires nothing and the charge is full at "max_time" (default 40), eased by "curve" (linear, ease_in, ease_out, ease_in_out). The beam then shows for "fire_time" (default 8), and with a "taper" from 0 to 1 it appears at full length and narrows to nothing over that fraction of the end of that time instead of retracting, and "grow" (default 0.15) is the fraction of the start over which it widens from nothing to full size. "shots" (default 1) fires that many shots "shot_interval" ticks apart (default 4), each aimed where you look at that moment, and "ignore_hit_immunity" lets every shot damage the same target. Each of the other settings is a { min, max } range used for damage, range, knockback and the amplifier and duration of the entity effects, from no charge to full charge. See the charged beam example.✗/<code>pierce</code>BooleanWhether the beam passes through every entity in its way and hits all of them, stopping only at a block or its max_distance.✗false<code>pierce_limit</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)With pierce, the most entities the beam passes through: it ends at the last one. 0 is no limit.✗0<code>pierce_full_charge_only</code>BooleanWith pierce and a charge, only a fully charged shot passes through entities; weaker shots stop at the first one.✗false<code>pierce_size</code>Pierce SizeWith pierce, how far in blocks the beam's reach extends sideways (width) and up and down (height) around the line, so a wide flat or tall thin slash can hit entities beside its path. Default 0.3 for both.✗/<code>knockback_distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far, in blocks, hit living entities are launched away from the caster (or the impact point), instead of the "knockback" strength. Knockback resistance weakens it.✗/<code>lift</code>(Dynamic) ValueUpward launch speed added by "knockback_distance" (0.4 is roughly a block and a half).✗/<code>airborne_lift</code>(Dynamic) ValueUpward launch speed used instead of "lift" while the caster is not on the ground.✗/<code>lateral_pull</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far, in blocks, hit living entities are pulled sideways across the look direction toward the aim line, on top of any knockback. Knockback resistance weakens it.✗/<code>armor_penetration</code>FloatThe fraction from 0 to 1 of a hit entity's armor ignored by the damage.✗0.0<code>heavy_armor</code>Heavy ArmorAdds "bonus" damage to hit entities whose armor value is at least "threshold".✗/<code>impact</code>ImpactMakes the beam burst where it ends: every living entity within "radius" blocks of that point is hit instead of the entities on the line, launched away from the point, with damage reduced by up to "falloff" (0 to 1) at the edge.✗/<code>visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle effects spawned when the beam fires, for beams that should look like air or smoke instead of a laser. "shape" is "streak" (particles along the beam every "step" blocks with "spread" jitter), "helix" ("strands" spirals of "radius" and "pitch" along the beam), "ring" ("rings" rings up to "radius" with "count" particles each, only "arc" degrees facing forward if under 360), "sphere" ("count" particles on a sphere of "radius") or "burst" (the same, filled). "crescent" draws crescent-shaped arcs of "count" particles along the beam every "step" blocks, spanning "arc" degrees (150 by default), sideways or up and down by "orientation" ("horizontal" or "vertical"). "anchor" is "end" (where the beam ends, default) or "caster" for rings, "height" raises them, and "speed" sends the particles along the beam or outward.✗/<code>entity_effects</code>Beam Effect[]Mob effects given to every living entity the beam hits. Duration is ticks or a time like "5s" (default 5s), amplifier 0 is level one, particles defaults to false.✗/<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDDamage type ID the damage is dealt as. Unset, it is a player attack for players and a mob attack otherwise.✗/<code>damage_type_overrides</code>Damage Type Override[]Damage types used instead of "damage_type" while their condition is true. Checked in order, first match wins. See the damage type overrides example.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>cone</code> (Cone)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>start_size</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The width of the cone at the origin, in blocks.✗/<code>end_size</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The width of the cone at its far end, in blocks.✗/<code>end_distance</code>Float (0.01 ~ 512.0)The distance in blocks at which the cone reaches its end size.✗/<code>rays</code>Integer (1 ~ 128)How many rays are cast to cover the cone.✗/</p> <p><p><code>block_mode</code> (Block Mode)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>type</code><code>melt</code><code>freeze</code>Whether blocks hit by the beam melt or freeze.✓/<code>time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long a block takes to change.✗60<code>auto_time</code>BooleanIf true, the time is worked out from the block instead of using a fixed value.✗false<code>auto_min_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The shortest automatic time.✗10<code>auto_max_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The longest automatic time.✗200<code>speed_multiplier</code>(Dynamic) ValueMultiplies how fast blocks change.✗/<code>modifiers</code>Time Modifier[]Changes the time for specific blocks or limits the effect to them.✗/<code>conversions</code>Block Conversion[]Converts specific blocks into other blocks.✗/<code>particle</code>Particle EffectParticles shown on the changed blocks.✗/<code>frozen_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long frozen blocks stay frozen (freeze only).✗200<code>frozen_time_multiplier</code>(Dynamic) ValueMultiplies the frozen time (freeze only).✗/<code>slippery</code>BooleanWhether frozen blocks are slippery (freeze only).✗true<code>friction</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)The slipperiness of frozen blocks (freeze only).✗0.989<code>snow_layers</code>Snow LayersSnow that builds up on frozen blocks (freeze only).✗/</p> <p><p><code>block_mode.modifiers[]</code> (Time Modifier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>type</code><code>whitelist</code><code>blacklist</code>A whitelist only affects the listed blocks, a blacklist leaves them out.✓/<code>blocks</code>Block ID(s) / TagThe blocks this entry covers.✓/<code>time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Overrides the time for these blocks.✗/</p> <p><p><code>block_mode.conversions[]</code> (Block Conversion)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>blocks</code>Block ID(s) / TagThe blocks that are converted.✓/<code>result</code>IdentifierThe block they turn into.✓/<code>revert</code>BooleanWhether the block changes back afterwards.✗true</p> <p><p><code>block_mode.particle</code> (Particle Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle to spawn.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)How many particles spawn.✗/<code>spread</code>DoubleHow far the particles spread from the origin.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>offset</code>Vector 3DOffset from the origin in blocks.✗/</p> <p><p><code>block_mode.snow_layers</code> (Snow Layers)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>max</code>Integer (0 ~ 8)The most snow layers that can build up.✗4<code>time_per_layer</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long one layer stays.✗100<code>interval</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The delay between new layers.✗20</p> <p><p><code>charge</code> (Beam Charge)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>min_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The shortest charge that still fires.✗/<code>max_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The charge time at which the beam is at full power.✗/<code>fire_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the beam keeps firing after the charge is released.✗8<code>taper</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)How much the beam thins out over its firing time.✗0.0<code>grow</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)How much the beam swells at the start of firing.✗0.15<code>shots</code>Integer (1 ~ 64)How many shots a single charge releases.✗/<code>shot_interval</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The delay between shots.✗/<code>ignore_hit_immunity</code>BooleanIf true, every shot can hurt even while the target is invulnerable from a previous hit.✗/<code>curve</code><code>linear</code><code>ease_in</code><code>ease_out</code><code>ease_in_out</code>How the charge amount maps onto the ranges below.✗/<code>damage</code>Charge RangeScales the damage with the charge.✗/<code>max_distance</code>Charge RangeScales the beam length with the charge.✗/<code>knockback</code>Charge RangeScales the knockback with the charge.✗/<code>effect_amplifier</code>Charge RangeScales the effect level with the charge.✗/<code>effect_duration</code>Charge Time RangeScales the effect duration with the charge.✗/</p> <p><p><code>charge.damage</code> (Charge Range)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>min</code>FloatThe value at the shortest charge.✓/<code>max</code>FloatThe value at a full charge.✓/</p> <p><p><code>charge.effect_duration</code> (Charge Time Range)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>min</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The duration at the shortest charge.✓/<code>max</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The duration at a full charge.✓/</p> <p><p><code>pierce_size</code> (Pierce Size)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>width</code>Float (0.0 ~ 16.0)The width of the piercing area in blocks.✓/<code>height</code>Float (0.0 ~ 16.0)The height of the piercing area in blocks.✓/</p> <p><p><code>heavy_armor</code> (Heavy Armor)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>threshold</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1000.0)The armor value of a target above which it counts as heavily armored.✓/<code>bonus</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1000.0)The extra amount added against heavily armored targets.✓/</p> <p><p><code>impact</code> (Impact)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>radius</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The radius of the impact in blocks.✓/<code>falloff</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)How much the strength drops towards the edge of the radius.✗/</p> <p><p><code>visuals[]</code> (Beam Visual)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>streak</code><code>helix</code><code>ring</code><code>sphere</code><code>burst</code><code>crescent</code>The particle pattern to draw.✓/<code>anchor</code><code>end</code><code>caster</code>Whether the pattern is drawn at the end of the beam or around the caster.✗/<code>orientation</code><code>horizontal</code><code>vertical</code>How ring and crescent patterns are turned.✗/<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle used.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 512)How many particles the pattern uses.✗/<code>radius</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The radius of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>step</code>Float (0.05 ~ 16.0)The spacing between particles along the beam.✗/<code>pitch</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The length of one full twist for helixes, in blocks.✗/<code>strands</code>Integer (1 ~ 8)How many strands a helix has.✗/<code>arc</code>Float (1.0 ~ 360.0)How much of a circle is drawn, in degrees.✗/<code>height</code>FloatThe height of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>rings</code>Integer (1 ~ 16)How many rings are drawn.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>spread</code>Float (0.0 ~ 8.0)How far the particles scatter.✗/</p> <p><p><code>entity_effects[]</code> (Beam Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)The effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/<code>size_tiers</code>Size Tier[]Changes or skips the effect depending on the width or type of the target.✗/</p> <p><p><code>entity_effects[].size_tiers[]</code> (Size Tier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>tag</code>Entity Type TagOnly entities in this tag use the tier.✗/<code>min_width</code>Double (0.0 ~ 64.0)The tier applies to entities at least this wide, in blocks.✗0.0<code>skip</code>BooleanIf true, matching entities do not get the effect at all.✗false<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDReplaces the effect for matching entities.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)Replaces the amplifier for matching entities.✗/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Replaces the duration for matching entities.✗/</p> <p><p><code>damage_type_overrides[]</code> (Damage Type Override)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>condition</code>Condition,Condition[]The conditions under which the override is used.✓/<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDThe damage type used instead.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
