ID<code>argon:invisibility</code> Makes the player invisible. Also makes mobs not see the player anymore. Adds a "fade" style for the transition. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>opacity</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)Opacity for other players/observers once fully invisible (0 = fully invisible).✗0.0<code>opacity_self</code>FloatOpacity for the local player's own view once fully invisible.✗0.2<code>mob_visibility_modifier</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)Multiplier fed into mob-sight/visibility checks once fully invisible.✗0.0<code>fade</code><code>default</code><code>energy</code>How the invisibility transition is visualized. "default" matches Palladium's own fade exactly. "energy" spreads an irregular, glowing energy boundary across the model's surface as it fades in/out instead of a uniform opacity change.✗default<code>energy_color</code>ColorOnly for "fade": "energy". The color of the glowing edge of the transition. Its hottest point still turns toward white.✗#6FEAFF<code>energy_additional_textures</code>string[]Only for "fade": "energy". Texture path prefixes (e.g. "mypack:textures/entity/suits/") of OTHER render layers that should dissolve and tint with the skin. Worn armor and suit textures are found automatically.✗[]</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:invisibility",
  "energy_additional_textures": "mypack:textures/entity/suits/"
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "invisibility": {
      "type": "argon:invisibility",
      "energy_additional_textures": "mypack:textures/entity/suits/"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

