ID<code>argon:light_source</code> While enabled, a real light-emitting block follows the entity (only in air or water, removed on disable) with colored particles, since block light has no color. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>light_level</code>Integer (0 ~ 15)How bright the emitted light is, from 0 (none) to 15 (maximum, matching a torch or brighter).✗15<code>particles</code>Light Particle,Light Particle[]One or more particle effects (a bare object or a list) spawned around the entity every tick, each with its own "color" (defaults to a warm torch-like tone when unset), "count" (particles per tick, default 3), "offset" ([x, y, z] added to the entity's position, default [0, 0.5, 0]), and "spread" ([x, y, z] random scatter radius per axis, default [0.2, 0.2, 0.2]). Configuring several entries lets you layer differently colored/positioned effects at once; an empty list disables particles entirely, leaving only the real light.✗/</p> <p><p><code>particles</code> (Light Particle)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>color</code>ColorThe color of the particle.✗/<code>count</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many particles spawn.✗/<code>offset</code>Vector 3DOffset from the origin in blocks.✗/<code>spread</code>Vector 3DHow far the particles spread on each axis.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
