ID<code>argon:lightning</code> On activation, strikes the block or entity the user looks at with a lightning-like beam that damages nearby living entities. Uses maximum range if the raycast hits nothing. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>DoubleThe maximum distance, in blocks, the raycast can reach when finding a block or entity to strike.✓/<code>beam_renderer</code>IdentifierThe beam renderer id used to draw the strike, e.g. one under data//palladium/beams/.✓/<code>damage</code>FloatThe damage dealt to living entities near the impact point, or none by default.✗0.0<code>damage_radius</code>DoubleHow far from the impact point, in blocks, entities can still take damage.✗2.0<code>duration_ticks</code>IntegerHow many ticks the beam visual stays on screen.✗10<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDA damage type ID such as "minecraft:magic" or one from a pack. Left unset, it is a player attack when a player uses this and a mob attack otherwise. Unknown types fall back to that.✗/ <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:lightning",
