ID<code>argon:heal</code> On its first enabled tick, heals the user, the ally they are looking at, or every ally nearby. Allies are the user, their team members and their pets. Gives an exact instant amount and can also apply effects such as regeneration. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>mode</code><code>self</code><code>look_target</code><code>area_allies</code>Who is healed: the user, the ally looked at (look_target), or every ally within range (area_allies).✗SELF<code>range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far away the looked-at ally can be, or the radius for area_allies, in blocks.✗12.0<code>instant</code>(Dynamic) ValueHealth restored at once, in half hearts (2 is one heart).✗0<code>effects</code>Beam Effect[]Effects applied to everyone healed, such as regeneration for healing over time (regeneration level 2 heals about 1 health per 25 ticks).✗/<code>self_pitch</code>DoubleIn look_target mode, looking down at least this many degrees heals the user instead of looking for an ally.✗60.0<code>fallback_self</code>BooleanIn look_target mode, heal the user when no ally is being looked at. Otherwise nothing happens.✗true<code>include_self</code>BooleanIn area_allies mode, whether the user is healed too.✗true<code>particles</code>Particle Effect[]Particles played at the middle of everyone healed.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>effects[]</code> (Beam Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)The effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/<code>size_tiers</code>Size Tier[]Changes or skips the effect depending on the width or type of the target.✗/</p> <p><p><code>effects[].size_tiers[]</code> (Size Tier)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>tag</code>Entity Type TagOnly entities in this tag use the tier.✗/<code>min_width</code>Double (0.0 ~ 64.0)The tier applies to entities at least this wide, in blocks.✗0.0<code>skip</code>BooleanIf true, matching entities do not get the effect at all.✗false<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDReplaces the effect for matching entities.✗/<code>amplifier</code>Integer (0 ~ 255)Replaces the amplifier for matching entities.✗/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Replaces the duration for matching entities.✗/</p> <p><p><code>particles[]</code> (Particle Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle to spawn.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)How many particles spawn.✗/<code>spread</code>DoubleHow far the particles spread from the origin.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>offset</code>Vector 3DOffset from the origin in blocks.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
