ID<code>argon:throwable_item</code> Throws the configured item from the holder's hand as a physical projectile that looks like the item, keeping its exact ItemStack (components, enchantments, durability) in a saved server record so it can never be duplicated or lost. Activating the ability again while the item is out recalls it (when recall_enabled). The projectile can bounce or embed in blocks, damage and pass through entities, return on its own after configured triggers, hit things on the way back, and be caught by its owner. Almost every number is a Value, so power progression can change it between throws. Values are read when the item is thrown, except the return_* settings and catch_radius, which are read again when the item is recalled. The item is restored to its original slot (or the inventory, or the ground) when caught, picked up, or when the owner logs out, dies or changes dimension. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>item</code>Item ID(s) / TagThe item, items or #tag the ability can throw, e.g. "fsang:mjolnir" or ["minecraft:diamond_sword"].✓/<code>hand</code><code>main_hand</code><code>off_hand</code><code>either</code>Which hand to take the item from.✗main_hand<code>pickup</code>Throwable PickupWhether and how the owner picks the item up again.✗/<code>throw</code>Throw SettingsHow the item is thrown and how far it can fly.✗/<code>combat</code>Throw CombatWhat the item does to entities it hits.✗/<code>block_impact</code>Throw Block ImpactWhat the item does when it hits a block.✗/<code>return</code>Throw ReturnHow and when the item comes back to its owner.✗/<code>render</code>Throw RenderHow the thrown item looks.✗/<code>sounds</code>Throw SoundsSounds for each stage of the throw. All are optional sound ids from sounds.json.✗/<code>targeting</code>Throw TargetingHow the item picks a target.✗/<code>homing</code>Throw HomingHow the item steers towards its target.✗/<code>ricochet</code>Throw RicochetLets the item jump to further targets after a hit.✗/<code>steering</code>Throw SteeringLets the owner steer the item in flight while an argon:throw_steer ability is held.✗/<code>camera</code>Throw CameraThe camera used when the steering mode is projectile_camera.✗/<code>perfect_catch</code>Throw Perfect CatchA bonus for catching the item at the right moment.✗/<code>pin</code>Throw PinPins a hit entity to a wall behind it.✗/<code>deflection</code>Throw DeflectionLets the item knock projectiles aside while it flies.✗/</p> <p><p><code>pickup</code> (Throwable Pickup)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>on_touch</code>BooleanThe owner picks the item up by walking near it while it is embedded or resting.✗true<code>radius</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow close the owner has to get to pick it up, in blocks.✗1.5</p> <p><p><code>throw</code> (Throw Settings)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>speed</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe speed of the throw.✗1.8<code>gravity_mode</code><code>none</code><code>vanilla</code><code>scaled</code>How gravity affects the item. None ignores gravity, vanilla uses the normal pull, scaled uses the gravity multiplier.✗vanilla<code>gravity</code>(Dynamic) ValueMultiplier for the scaled gravity mode.✗1.0<code>drag</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow much speed is kept each tick.✗0.99<code>inaccuracy</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far the throw direction can scatter.✗0.0<code>inherit_owner_velocity</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow much of the owner's own movement is added to the throw.✗0.35<code>maximum_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The longest the item can fly.✗200<code>maximum_distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe farthest the item can fly from where it was thrown, in blocks.✗96.0<code>maximum_owner_distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe farthest the item can get from its owner, in blocks.✗128.0<code>out_of_range</code><code>return</code><code>recover</code><code>drop</code>What happens when a limit is reached. The item is never deleted.✗return<code>windup</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The delay before release, so an animation can play.✗0</p> <p><p><code>combat</code> (Throw Combat)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>damage</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe damage dealt on a hit.✗6.0<code>knockback</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe knockback dealt on a hit.✗0.6<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDThe damage type used.✗/<code>maximum_targets</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow many entities one throw can hit. 0 means unlimited.✗1.0<code>entity_impact</code><code>continue</code><code>bounce</code><code>return</code><code>stop</code><code>embed</code>What the item does after hitting an entity. Embed lodges it in the mob, which it follows until recalled.✗continue<code>allow_repeat_targets</code>BooleanWhether the same entity can be hit more than once.✗false<code>rehit_cooldown</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long until an entity can be hit again.✗10</p> <p><p><code>block_impact</code> (Throw Block Impact)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>mode</code><code>bounce</code><code>embed</code><code>return</code><code>drop</code><code>stop</code>What the item does when it hits a block.✗embed<code>restitution</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow much speed a bounce keeps.✗0.6<code>friction</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow much speed is kept while sliding along a block.✗0.85<code>maximum_bounces</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow many times the item can bounce.✗3.0<code>embed_depth</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow deep the item sinks into the block, in blocks.✗0.3<code>embed_duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the item stays embedded. 0 means until recalled or picked up.✗0</p> <p><p><code>return</code> (Throw Return)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>triggers</code><code>none</code><code>after_hit</code><code>after_block_impact</code><code>after_timeout</code><code>after_distance</code><code>always</code>,<code>none</code><code>after_hit</code><code>after_block_impact</code><code>after_timeout</code><code>after_distance</code><code>always</code>[]What makes the item return on its own.✗[ "after_hit" ]<code>timeout</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)Return after this long when the timeout trigger is used.✗60<code>distance</code>(Dynamic) ValueReturn after this distance in blocks when the distance trigger is used.✗32.0<code>speed</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe speed of the return.✗2.4<code>acceleration</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow quickly the return speeds up.✗0.3<code>turn_rate</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow fast the item steers towards its owner, in degrees per tick.✗30.0<code>accuracy</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow precisely the item steers, from 0 to 100.✗100.0<code>maximum_duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)A safety limit for the return flight.✗200<code>block_collision</code><code>pass_through</code><code>stop</code>Whether the returning item passes through blocks or stops at them.✗stop<code>damage_enabled</code>BooleanWhether the item hurts entities on the way back.✗false<code>damage_multiplier</code>(Dynamic) ValueMultiplies the damage on the way back.✗1.0<code>maximum_damage_targets</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow many entities the return can hit. 0 means unlimited.✗0.0<code>catch_radius</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow close to the owner the item counts as caught, in blocks.✗1.25<code>recall</code>BooleanActivating the ability again while the item is out recalls it.✗false</p> <p><p><code>render</code> (Throw Render)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>scale</code>FloatThe size of the item model.✗1.0<code>rotation_mode</code><code>none</code><code>spin</code><code>tumble</code>How the item turns in flight.✗spin<code>rotation_speed</code>FloatHow fast the item turns, in degrees per tick.✗36.0<code>rotation_axis</code><code>x</code><code>y</code><code>z</code>The axis the item turns around.✗x<code>rotation_offset</code>Vector 3DA fixed rotation added to the model, as [x, y, z] degrees.✗[ 0, 0, 0 ]<code>face_velocity</code>BooleanWhether the item points along its flight direction.✗true<code>embed_spin_angle</code>FloatThe angle the item sits at while embedded, in degrees.✗0.0<code>embed_shift</code>FloatHow far the model is moved along the throw direction while embedded in a block. Negative values pull it back out of the surface.✗0.0</p> <p><p><code>sounds</code> (Throw Sounds)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>throw</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item is thrown.✗/<code>entity_hit</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item hits an entity.✗/<code>block_hit</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item hits a block.✗/<code>recall</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item is recalled.✗/<code>return</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item starts returning.✗/<code>catch</code>IdentifierPlayed when the item is caught.✗/<code>flight</code>IdentifierLoops while the item is flying.✗/</p> <p><p><code>targeting</code> (Throw Targeting)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>mode</code><code>none</code><code>automatic</code><code>marked</code><code>hybrid</code>How targets are picked. Marked uses targets set with the mark ability, hybrid combines both.✗none<code>accuracy</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe chance of each acquisition attempt succeeding, from 0 to 100.✗100.0<code>detection_range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far away targets are found, in blocks.✗16.0<code>cone</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe width of the search cone in front of the item, in degrees.✗90.0<code>line_of_sight</code>BooleanWhether targets have to be visible.✗true<code>filter</code><code>hostile</code><code>living</code><code>players</code><code>non_players</code>Which kinds of entities can be targeted.✗hostile<code>entity_types</code>Entity Type ID(s) / TagLimits targets to these entity types or tags.✗/<code>priority</code><code>nearest</code><code>look_direction</code><code>lowest_health</code><code>random</code><code>marked_order</code>How one target is chosen from several.✗nearest</p> <p><p><code>homing</code> (Throw Homing)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>accuracy</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow precisely the item steers, from 0 to 100, independent of acquisition.✗100.0<code>turn_rate</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow fast the item turns, in degrees per tick.✗14.0<code>acceleration</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow quickly the item speeds up while homing.✗0.0<code>max_speed</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe top speed while homing. 0 means no limit.✗0.0<code>prediction</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far ahead of a moving target the item aims.✗0.0<code>target_offset</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe height on the target's body that is aimed at, as a fraction.✗0.5<code>lost_target</code><code>continue</code><code>reacquire</code><code>return</code>What happens when the target is lost.✗continue</p> <p><p><code>ricochet</code> (Throw Ricochet)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>enabled</code>BooleanWhether the item jumps to another target after a hit.✗false<code>maximum</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow many ricochets are allowed. 0 means one fewer than the maximum targets.✗0.0<code>target_range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far the next target can be, in blocks.✗10.0<code>speed</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe speed between targets.✗2.6<code>turn_rate</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow fast the item turns towards the next target, in degrees per tick.✗40.0<code>damage_multiplier</code>(Dynamic) ValueMultiplies the damage of ricochet hits.✗1.0</p> <p><p><code>steering</code> (Throw Steering)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>mode</code><code>none</code><code>look_direction</code><code>projectile_camera</code>How the owner steers the item while an argon:throw_steer ability is held.✗none<code>turn_rate</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow fast the item turns, in degrees per tick.✗10.0<code>strength</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow strongly the steering input is applied.✗1.0<code>maximum_speed</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe top speed while steering. 0 means the throw speed.✗0.0<code>acceleration</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow quickly the item speeds up while steering.✗0.08<code>return_on