ID<code>argon:path_vision</code> Client only. Shows where nearby entities and projectiles are heading: a mob's AI route, a short prediction for other movers, a projectile's predicted flight. Drawn as a trail, changes nothing. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>detection_radius</code>Double (1.0 ~ 256.0)How far from the holder, in blocks, entities and projectiles are looked for. Only loaded entities are ever considered.✗24.0<code>max_targets</code>Integer (1 ~ 128)The most targets shown at once. Which ones are kept when there are more is decided by target_priority.✗16<code>target_priority</code><code>closest</code><code>hostile_first</code><code>projectiles_first</code>Which targets are kept when more than max_targets are in range and which come first: "closest" orders by distance, "hostile_first" puts hostile mobs before everything else, "projectiles_first" puts projectiles first. Within a group the closest come first.✗closest<code>path_update_interval</code>Integer (1 ~ 40)How often paths are recalculated. Between updates the trail follows the target smoothly, and a new navigation path from the server updates it immediately.✗2<code>max_path_length</code>Double (1.0 ~ 512.0)The longest stretch of path shown, measured along the path itself from the target.✗32.0<code>track</code>string[]What is shown, mixing categories ("players", "hostile", "passive", "neutral", "projectiles", "mobs", "all") with entity type ids and "#tags". Listed types and tags are tracked whatever their category. An unknown entry stops the power from loading.✗[ "players", "hostile", "neutral", "projectiles" ]<code>ignore</code>string[]Anything that matches here is never shown, even when it matches track. Takes the same entries as track.✗[]<code>show_entity_paths</code>BooleanWhether paths are shown for mobs and players.✗true<code>predict_entity_movement</code>BooleanWhether an entity with no active path gets a physics prediction from its recent velocity. It is an estimate, not a destination, and assumes the entity keeps going the way it is going.✗true<code>entity_prediction_time</code>Double (0.1 ~ 10.0)How far ahead entity movement is predicted. Longer predictions get less reliable.✗2.0<code>show_projectile_paths</code>BooleanWhether the flight of projectiles is shown.✗true<code>projectile_prediction_time</code>Double (0.1 ~ 10.0)How far ahead a projectile's flight is simulated. The path also stops at the first expected collision.✗3.0<code>show_projectile_impact</code>BooleanWhether a particle marks where a projectile is expected to hit. Nothing shows when no impact is predicted.✗true<code>show_time_to_impact</code>BooleanWhether the time left before the predicted impact is written above the impact point, such as 0.8s.✗false<code>impact_particle</code>ParticleThe particle that marks the predicted impact, as a particle type ID or a particle object.✗minecraft:end_rod<code>preview_aimed_shots</code>BooleanShows the path a shot would take while its shooter aims (a drawn bow, ready trident or loaded crossbow) instead of following fired projectiles. Ends at the first block or tracked entity hit and uses projectile_trail. Fireworks aren't predicted.✗false<code>aim_charge_color</code>Colorpreview_aimed_shots only. The aim line's color when the draw has just started, shifting to the projectile trail's color as the shot gets ready. Set it to the trail's color to turn the shift off.✗#FFD23F<code>entity_trail</code>IdentifierThe Palladium trail (palladium/trails/.json) that draws entity paths. Its renderer, lifetime, offset and spacing set the look.✗argon:path_vision_entity<code>projectile_trail</code>IdentifierThe Palladium trail that draws projectile paths, set up like entity_trail so projectiles can look different from entities. Defaults to "argon:path_vision_projectile".✗argon:path_vision_projectile<code>trail_render_distance</code>Double (4.0 ~ 512.0)Paths of targets farther than this from the camera are not drawn.✗64.0<code>trail_smoothing</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)How much navigation corners are rounded. A rounded stretch that would pass through a block is left sharp instead.✗0.7<code>render_through_walls</code>BooleanWhether the trail can be seen through blocks. Applies to trails drawn with Palladium's laser render types, which includes the gradient and lightning trails.✗false <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:path_vision",
  "detection_radius": 24,
  "max_targets": 16,
  "entity_trail": "argon:path_vision_entity",
  "projectile_trail": "argon:path_vision_projectile",
  "show_time_to_impact": true,
  "track": [
    "hostile",
    "projectiles",
    "minecraft:villager"
  ],
  "ignore": [
    "#minecraft:undead"
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
