ID<code>argon:projectile_effect</code> Shoots a projectile like the built-in projectile ability, and can also give one or more status effects to the living entity it hits. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>entity_type</code>Entity Type IDID of an entity type (must be a projectile).✓/<code>entity_data</code>NBTAdditional NBT data for the projectile entity.✗/<code>inaccuracy</code>(Dynamic) ValueInaccuracy when shooting the projectile. A value, so it can change with conditions (for example a wider spread while overloaded).✗0<code>velocity</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)Velocity with which the projectile is being shot.✗1.5<code>swinging_arm</code><code>none</code><code>main_arm</code><code>off_arm</code><code>right_arm</code><code>left_arm</code><code>both</code>The arm which will swing when the projectile is being shot.✗MAIN_ARM<code>ignore_player_movement</code>BooleanNormally the player's current velocity is added to the projectile's velocity. This turns that off.✗false<code>offset</code>Vector 3DA [x, y, z] spawn offset, relative to the entity's facing direction. Defaults to [0, 0, 0].✗(0.0, 0.0, 0.0)<code>hit_effects</code>Projectile Hit Effect,Projectile Hit Effect[]Each entry configures its own effect, duration, amplifier, particles, and powers* (a list of {power, mode} entries, where "power" is an explicit power id, a power tag ("#namespace:tag"), or a mix of both - "include" requires a matching power, "exclude" forbids one) - all entries are granted to whatever living entity the projectile directly hits. Empty by default, meaning no effect is granted.✓/<code>item_tint</code>Item TintOnly meaningful for an entity_type whose appearance includes an "item" appearance (e.g. "palladium:custom_projectile"). Tints every such appearance's item using whatever colour a registered source reads off an item in "slot" (a Palladium player slot, e.g. "mainhand", "curios:hands" - every item currently in that slot is checked, and the first one "source" finds a colour on wins), the same way a dyed item is tinted - so this only has a visible effect if the appearance item's own model has a tint-indexed layer to begin with. An id nothing has registered, or no matching item in the slot, silently leaves the appearance untinted; omit "item_tint" entirely for a projectile that should never be tinted.✗/<code>max_range</code>DoubleIf above 0, the projectile disappears once it has flown this many blocks from where it was shot.✗0<code>sprint_interrupt</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)If above 0, a living entity the projectile hits cannot sprint for this long.✗0</p> <p><p><code>hit_effects</code> (Projectile Hit Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✓/<code>amplifier</code>IntegerThe effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/<code>powers</code>Power Requirement,Power Requirement[]Only targets that match these power requirements get the effect.✗/</p> <p><p><code>hit_effects.powers</code> (Power Requirement)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>power</code>Power ID(s) / TagThe power or powers the entity has to have.✓/<code>mode</code><code>include</code><code>exclude</code>Whether the entity must have the power (include) or must not have it (exclude).✗include</p> <p><p><code>item_tint</code> (Item Tint)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>slot</code><code>mainhand</code><code>offhand</code><code>head</code><code>chest</code><code>legs</code><code>feet</code><code>body</code><code>curios:head</code><code>curios:necklace</code>The slot of the item that is tinted.✓/<code>source</code>IdentifierThe tint source used.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
