ID<code>argon:reconstruction</code> On activation, matches the item in "target_slot" against "reconstructions" and uses up the first match with enough input to make its result. With "recipe", hold to browse crafting recipes for the held item and release to swap. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>reconstructions</code>Reconstruction Entry[],<code>recipe</code>The ordered list of input-to-result conversions this ability can perform, or the literal string "recipe" to browse crafting table recipes that use the held item instead. In recipe mode every other ingredient is ignored and only the held item is consumed.✓/<code>target_slot</code><code>mainhand</code><code>offhand</code><code>head</code><code>chest</code><code>legs</code><code>feet</code><code>body</code><code>curios:head</code><code>curios:necklace</code>Which slot's item is checked and consumed; defaults to the main hand.✗mainhand<code>conversion_mode</code><code>single</code><code>maximum</code><code>fixed</code>SINGLE applies the matched recipe once, MAXIMUM as many times as the input allows, FIXED up to "fixed_amount" times. Ignored in recipe mode.✗SINGLE<code>fixed_amount</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many times to apply the recipe when conversion_mode is FIXED. Ignored in recipe mode.✗1<code>overflow_behavior</code><code>fail</code><code>drop</code>FAIL cancels the whole conversion if the result can't fully fit in the inventory. DROP inserts what fits and drops the rest at the user's feet.✗FAIL<code>component_policy</code><code>result_only</code><code>copy_safe</code><code>copy_all</code>RESULT_ONLY uses exactly the result's components. COPY_SAFE also copies cosmetic ones (name, lore, dye color, custom model data) from the input. COPY_ALL copies every component that differs from the item's defaults.✗RESULT_ONLY</p> <p><p><code>reconstructions[]</code> (Reconstruction Entry)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>input</code>Ingredient / ItemThe item or tag that is used up.✓/<code>input_amount</code>Integer (&gt; 0)How many of the input are used up.✗1<code>result</code>Item / ItemStackThe item stack that is made.✓/<code>result_amount</code>Integer (&gt; 0)Overrides the amount of the result.✗/<code>priority</code>IntegerEntries with a higher priority are checked first.✗0</p> <pre><code>{
