ID<code>argon:seek_strike</code> On activation, picks up to "max_targets" living entities around the user and rushes between them one after another, hitting each once with fixed damage and knockback. Allies are skipped, and a target is skipped when solid blocks are in the way. The user stays beside the last target. All Values are read once on activation. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow far from the user targets can be chosen, in blocks.✓/<code>max_targets</code>(Dynamic) ValueHow many targets are hit at most. Each can only be hit once.✗1<code>damage</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe final damage of each hit. The user's attack damage is not added.✓/<code>damage_type</code>Damage Type IDThe damage type used; a player attack when left out.✗/<code>knockback</code>(Dynamic) ValueKnockback strength of each hit, where 0.4 is a normal hit.✗0<code>lift</code>(Dynamic) ValueUpward velocity added to every hit target.✗0.2<code>speed</code>DoubleHow many blocks per tick the user travels towards a target.✗2.5<code>reach</code>DoubleHow close, in blocks, the user gets to a target before striking.✗1.8<code>aim</code><code>look</code><code>nearest</code><code>marked</code>"look" picks the entity under the crosshair first, otherwise the nearest one inside cone_angle. "nearest" starts from the entity closest to the user. "marked" only goes for the user's argon:target_mark target (hostile_only is ignored, and nothing happens without a mark).✗look<code>cone_angle</code>DoubleThe full opening angle of the look cone, in degrees.✗90.0<code>hostile_only</code>BooleanIf true, only hostile mobs and other players can be picked.✗true<code>end_effects</code>Potion Hit Effect,Potion Hit Effect[]Effects applied to the user after the last hit, for example a short slowdown.✗[]<code>hit_visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle visuals spawned at each target when it is hit, in the same format as the visuals of argon:energy_beam.✗[]<code>travel_visuals</code>Beam Visual[]Particle visuals spawned along every step of the rush, for example a streak.✗[]<code>hit_sound</code>IdentifierA sound event played at every target when it is hit, instead of the default hit sound.✗/<code>hit_sound_volume</code>FloatVolume of hit_sound.✗1.0<code>hit_sound_pitch</code>FloatPitch of hit_sound.✗0.9<code>hit_effects</code>Potion Hit Effect,Potion Hit Effect[]Effects applied to every target that is hit, for example a short slowdown that interrupts its movement.✗[]<code>consume_mark</code>BooleanIf true, a hit on the user's marked target ends the mark.✗false<code>execute_threshold</code>DoubleA target at or below this health fraction (0 to 1) takes execute_bonus extra damage. 0 disables it.✗0.0<code>execute_bonus</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe extra damage dealt to a target under execute_threshold.✗0<code>dash</code>BooleanIf true and no target was chosen, the user dashes straight along the look direction for up to range blocks (stopping at walls) and strikes the first valid entity it touches. Not used with aim marked.✗false<code>exit_speed</code>DoubleSpeed in blocks per tick the user keeps along the last movement direction when the rush ends, instead of stopping dead.✗0.0</p> <p><p><code>end_effects</code> (Potion Hit Effect)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>effect</code>Mob Effect IDThe effect to apply.✓/<code>duration</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the effect lasts.✓/<code>amplifier</code>IntegerThe effect level, starting at 0.✗/<code>max_amplifier</code>IntegerThe highest level repeated hits can stack the effect up to.✗/<code>particles</code>BooleanWhether the effect shows its particles.✗/</p> <p><p><code>hit_visuals[]</code> (Beam Visual)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>shape</code><code>streak</code><code>helix</code><code>ring</code><code>sphere</code><code>burst</code><code>crescent</code>The particle pattern to draw.✓/<code>anchor</code><code>end</code><code>caster</code>Whether the pattern is drawn at the end of the beam or around the caster.✗/<code>orientation</code><code>horizontal</code><code>vertical</code>How ring and crescent patterns are turned.✗/<code>particle</code>ParticleThe particle used.✓/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 512)How many particles the pattern uses.✗/<code>radius</code>Float (0.0 ~ 64.0)The radius of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>step</code>Float (0.05 ~ 16.0)The spacing between particles along the beam.✗/<code>pitch</code>Float (0.1 ~ 64.0)The length of one full twist for helixes, in blocks.✗/<code>strands</code>Integer (1 ~ 8)How many strands a helix has.✗/<code>arc</code>Float (1.0 ~ 360.0)How much of a circle is drawn, in degrees.✗/<code>height</code>FloatThe height of the pattern in blocks.✗/<code>rings</code>Integer (1 ~ 16)How many rings are drawn.✗/<code>speed</code>DoubleThe speed of the particles.✗/<code>spread</code>Float (0.0 ~ 8.0)How far the particles scatter.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:seek_strike",
  "range": 10,
  "max_targets": 1,
  "damage": 8,
  "knockback": 0.8,
  "lift": 0.2,
  "execute_bonus": 0,
  "properties": {
    "title": "Seek Strike"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
