</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:sensory_overload</code> While enabled, overwhelms the wearer's senses: a visual only warp, lagging camera, screen shake, activation flash, pulsing tint and muffled non-music sound. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>warp_intensity</code>FloatHow strong the nausea style screen warp is, 0 (none) to 2 (well past the vanilla effect). It copies the vanilla look directly and doesn't apply the real Nausea effect.✗1.0<code>drag_strength</code>FloatHow much the rendered view drags behind the wearer's real look direction, 0 (none) to 1 (heavy).✗0.6<code>shake_base_intensity</code>FloatThe weakest a single camera-shake pulse can be.✗0.1<code>shake_max_intensity</code>FloatThe strongest a single camera-shake pulse can be.✗0.4<code>flash_enabled</code>BooleanWhether a brief full-screen flash plays on activation.✗false<code>flash_color</code>ColorThe color of the activation flash, when flash_enabled is true.✗#FFFFFF<code>flash_fade_ticks</code>IntegerHow many ticks the activation flash takes to fade from full brightness to nothing.✗15<code>pulse_color</code>ColorThe color of the full-screen tint that pulses while enabled.✗#FFFFFF<code>pulse_opacity</code>FloatThe pulsing tint's peak opacity at the brightest point of each pulse.✗0.4<code>pulse_speed</code>FloatHow many pulses per second the full-screen tint cycles through.✗2.0<code>mute_volume</code>FloatVolume multiplier applied to non-music sounds while enabled, from 0 (silent) to 1 (unchanged).✗0.4</p> <pre><code>{
