ID<code>argon:state_selector</code> On activation, changes a block state property (e.g. "open", "lit", "facing") of the block you target, using "block_properties". With several entries, a held key scrolls a menu of the ones that apply. SettingsExample 1Example 2In a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>Integer (&gt; 0)The maximum distance, in blocks, the raycast can reach.✗8<code>block_filter</code>Block ID(s) / TagOptional whitelist of blocks (explicit IDs and/or tags) this ability can affect; if unset, any block is eligible.✗/<code>block_properties</code>State Selector Property,State Selector Property[]One or more properties to offer. A single entry applies immediately. Several entries open a scrollable picker.✓/<code>allow_block_entities</code>BooleanIf false (default), refuses to touch any block with a block entity (chests, furnaces, etc.) for safety.✗false<code>notify_neighbors</code>BooleanIf true (default), the change triggers normal neighbor updates (redstone, shape updates, etc). The client is always synced either way.✗true<code>require_valid_survival</code>BooleanIf true (default), the new state must be able to survive at that position or the change is cancelled.✗true<code>allow_multiblock</code>BooleanIf false (default), won't change structural multi-block properties ("half", "part", e.g. doors, beds, tall plants), since one half alone can desync the pair. Modded blocks with other names aren't all covered, use "block_filter" for those.✗false</p> <p><p><code>block_properties</code> (State Selector Property)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>property</code>StringThe name of the block state property, such as open, facing or waterlogged. Whatever the targeted block actually has is used.✓/<code>operation</code><code>set</code><code>next</code><code>previous</code><code>toggle</code>How the property changes.✓/<code>value</code>StringThe value used by the set operation, in its normal string form such as true, east or 3.✗/<code>allowed_values</code>String,String[]Restricts and orders the values this property may use.✗[]</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:state_selector",
  "block_properties": {
    "property": "open",
    "operation": "toggle"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:state_selector",
  "block_properties": [
    {
      "property": "facing",
      "operation": "next"
    },
    {
      "property": "waterlogged",
      "operation": "toggle"
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "state_selector": {
      "type": "argon:state_selector",
