ID<code>argon:charged_takeoff</code> Hold the Takeoff key (Controls &gt; Argon, unbound by default) to charge, release to launch. The longer you hold, the harder it throws you. One push, not flight. Pair it with argon:took_off to continue into flight. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>requires_ground</code>BooleanWhether charging can only begin on the ground (checked on the server).✗true<code>cancel_when_airborne</code>BooleanWhether a charge started on the ground is dropped once the player leaves it (walking off a ledge, jumping).✗true<code>allow_movement_while_charging</code>BooleanWhether the player can walk while charging. If false, walking speed is held at zero until they release or cancel.✗true<code>min_charge_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long the key must be held before releasing launches. Releasing sooner cancels, with no launch and no cooldown.✗4<code>max_charge_time</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long a full charge takes. Holding longer adds nothing, they stay fully charged until release.✗40<code>cooldown</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long after a launch before another can be charged. 0 for none. Cancelled charges don't start it.✗0<code>min_launch_strength</code>DoubleUpward speed, in blocks per tick, of the weakest launch (a normal jump is about 0.42). 0.6 gets roughly 2.7 blocks.✗0.6<code>max_launch_strength</code>DoubleUpward speed of a full charge, never exceeded. 1.7 gets roughly 15 blocks before gravity wins.✗1.7<code>flight_at_apex</code>BooleanStarts the player's palladium:flight at the top of the climb so they stay up. Needs an unlocked flight ability, does nothing without one.✗false<code>launch_direction</code><code>vertical</code><code>look_direction</code><code>hybrid</code>Which way the push goes: "vertical" (straight up), "look_direction" (where the player looks on release, same strength at any angle) or "hybrid" (up, bent toward the look direction by "directional_influence").✗vertical<code>minimum_launch_pitch</code>Doublelook_direction only. The lowest launch angle, in degrees above the horizon (negative is below). 0 never launches downward, -90 means no limit.✗-90.0<code>directional_influence</code>Doublehybrid only. 0 to 1, how much the look direction bends the launch away from straight up. Strongest looking level, nothing looking straight up or down. It never changes how hard the launch is, only where it points.✗0.35<code>minimum_upward_component</code>Doublehybrid only. 0 to 1, the least vertical share the launch may have, whatever the camera does. 0.5 keeps at least half the push pointing up, 1 is straight up.✗0.5<code>directional_launch_particles</code>BooleanWhether the burst of debris at launch is thrown away from the launch direction (backward for a forward launch) instead of spreading around the player.✗false<code>replace_velocity</code>BooleanWhether the push replaces the player's whole velocity. By default sideways speed is kept (never raised above what they had or max_launch_strength), so launches can't be chained into unlimited speed.✗false<code>charge_curve</code><code>linear</code><code>ease_in</code><code>ease_out</code><code>ease_in_out</code>How strength follows the charge: "linear", "ease_in" (weak early, much stronger near full), "ease_out" (strong early, small gains near full) or "ease_in_out".✗linear<code>charge_particles</code>Charge ParticlesDebris from the ground blocks around the player while charging. Keys: enabled (true), radius (2.5), count (4), interval (2 ticks), rise_speed (0.12), lifetime (24 ticks), scale (1), scales_with_charge (none, count, speed or both). Client-only.✗{}<code>launch_particles</code>Launch ParticlesDebris thrown up on launch, scaled by its strength. Keys: burst (true), count (40), radius (3), strength (0.4 blocks per tick).✗{}</p> <p><p><code>charge_particles</code> (Charge Particles)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>enabled</code>BooleanWhether particles show while charging.✗/<code>radius</code>Double (0.5 ~ 16.0)The radius particles gather from, in blocks.✗/<code>count</code>Integer (1 ~ 32)How many particles spawn each time.✗/<code>interval</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)The delay between spawns.✗/<code>rise_speed</code>Double (0.0 ~ 1.0)How fast the particles rise.✗/<code>lifetime</code>Integer,Time String ("40s", "2m", etc.)How long each particle lives.✗/<code>scale</code>Double (0.1 ~ 8.0)The size of the particles.✗/<code>scales_with_charge</code><code>none</code><code>count</code><code>speed</code><code>both</code>What grows as the charge builds.✗/</p> <p><p><code>launch_particles</code> (Launch Particles)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>burst</code>BooleanWhether a burst of particles is released on launch.✗/<code>count</code>Integer (0 ~ 200)How many particles are released.✗/<code>radius</code>Double (0.5 ~ 16.0)The radius of the burst in blocks.✗/<code>strength</code>Double (0.0 ~ 3.0)How fast the particles fly outward.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:charged_takeoff",
  "flight_at_apex": true,
