ID<code>argon:time_growth</code> Makes attributes grow stronger the longer the ability has been enabled for the player. Every enabled tick counts towards the ability's age (time spent offline or with the ability disabled does not count), and each entry adds "per_day" to its attribute for every day of age between "start_day" and "max_day". The age is available to other abilities through the argon:power_age value and condition. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>attributes</code>Growth Entry[]The attributes that grow, from 1 to 32 entries.✓/<code>ticks_per_day</code>IntegerHow many enabled ticks count as one day of age. 24000 is one Minecraft day, lower it to test growth quickly.✗24000<code>whole_days</code>BooleanIf true the bonus only increases once per full day. If false it grows smoothly.✗true<code>reset_on_death</code>BooleanIf true the age goes back to 0 when the player dies.✗true<code>reset_on_power_loss</code>BooleanIf true the age goes back to 0 when the player loses the power this ability belongs to.✗true<code>milestones</code>Growth Milestone[]Ages that announce themselves when the player reaches them by natural growth. They do not fire when the age is set with a command.✗[]</p> <p><p><code>attributes[]</code> (Growth Entry)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>attribute</code>Attribute IDThe attribute that grows.✓/<code>operation</code><code>add_value</code><code>add_multiplied_base</code><code>add_multiplied_total</code>How the bonus is applied to the attribute.✗add_value<code>per_day</code>DoubleThe bonus gained per day of age.✓/<code>start_day</code>Double (0.0 ~ 1000000.0)The day growth begins at.✗0.0<code>max_day</code>Double (0.0 ~ 1000000.0)The day growth stops at.✓/</p> <p><p><code>milestones[]</code> (Growth Milestone)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>day</code>Double (0.0 ~ 1000000.0)The day of age the milestone happens at.✓/<code>title</code>Text ComponentThe title shown on screen