ID<code>argon:wall_crawling</code> Lets the user climb flat vertical walls and optionally ceilings with look-relative WASD. Turns around outside corners on its own and rolls the camera so the attached surface reads as "down". SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>base_speed</code>FloatThe base crawling speed, in blocks per tick, before speed_multiplier is applied.✗0.13<code>speed_multiplier</code>FloatMultiplies base_speed, so different powers can reuse this ability at different crawl speeds (0.5 is half speed, 2.0 is double).✗1.0<code>attach_distance</code>FloatHow close to a wall or ceiling face the user must be to attach to (or remain attached to) it.✗0.5<code>detach_strength</code>FloatHow hard jumping off a surface pushes the user in whichever direction they're currently looking.✗0.3<code>gravity_pull_strength</code>FloatA small constant velocity into the attached surface every tick, whether or not the user is moving. The same solid block collision that stops it confirms the surface is still there, so there is no distance check.✗0.08<code>ceiling_crawling</code>BooleanWhether ceilings (not just vertical walls) are valid attachment surfaces.✗true<code>camera_roll</code>BooleanIf true, smoothly rolls the local user's camera so the attached surface reads as "down", making the wall or ceiling their floor and not just their movement plane.✗true<code>third_person_camera_roll</code>BooleanWhether camera_roll also applies in third person, not only first person. Off by default, since third person shows the user's own model and the roll doesn't reorient it.✗false<code>use_directional_gravity</code>BooleanIf true, attaching to a surface turns the player's gravity toward it (the surface becomes their floor, and the hitbox, camera and model turn with it) instead of steering velocity along it. The options below apply to this mode.✗false<code>gravity_strength</code>FloatA multiplier on normal gravity while attached; it is how firmly the player is held to the surface.✗1.0<code>rotate_camera</code>BooleanWhether the camera turns with the surface. If missing, camera_roll is used. When false the view stays upright to the world while the body and movement still turn.✗/<code>camera_transition_time</code>IntegerTicks the camera takes to turn to a new surface. 0 turns it at once.✗6<code>smooth_transitions</code>BooleanWhether the camera and body turn gradually. When false every turn is instant.✗true<code>transition_duration</code>IntegerTicks the drawn body takes to turn to a new surface.✗6<code>transition_easing</code>Stringlinear, ease_in, ease_out or ease_in_out: how the turns speed up and slow down.✗ease_in_out<code>view_orientation</code>StringWhat a turn between surfaces does to where the player looks. relative: same angles in the new gravity. world: angles are recomputed so the player keeps looking at the same point in the world.✗relative<code>surface_detection_range</code>FloatHow close a surface must be to grab or keep hold of it, in blocks. If missing, attach_distance is used.✗/<code>surface_transition_tolerance</code>FloatHow far before the edge of a surface the player starts turning round it, in blocks (0 to 0.3).✗0.15<code>movement_mode</code>Stringsurface_relative: W goes up the wall (or along the heading) whatever the camera does. camera_relative: W goes where the camera points, along the surface.✗surface_relative<code>surface_jump_strength</code>FloatHow hard jumping pushes the player straight off the surface. If missing, detach_strength is used.✗/<code>auto_crawl</code>BooleanWhether the player may turn onto surfaces where only a crawl sized body fits, crawling through tight spaces.✗true<code>allow_ceiling_crawling</code>BooleanWhether ceilings are valid surfaces. If missing, ceiling_crawling is used.✗/<code>allow_corner_transitions</code>BooleanWhether the player turns from one surface to the next at corners on their own (and from the floor onto a wall they walk into). When false they can only grab a surface from the air.✗true<code>preserve_surface_momentum</code>BooleanWhether speed is kept through a turn between surfaces.✗true<code>surface_speed_multiplier</code>FloatMultiplies the crawling speed (base_speed times speed_multiplier) on a surface only.✗1.0<code>allow_surface_sprinting</code>BooleanWhether sprinting makes the player crawl faster.✗true<code>crawl_when_not_sprinting</code>BooleanIf true, the player is crawl sized (the vanilla crawling pose, a 0.6 block hitbox that fits one block gaps) on a wall or ceiling unless sprinting. Sprinting stands them back up as far as there is room.✗false<code>play_running_animation</code>BooleanWhether sprinting along a wall or ceiling plays the running animation. Vanilla only starts it from ground movement, which doesn't happen while climbing. Only while sprinting.✗true</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:wall_crawling",
  "properties": {
    "title": "Wall Crawling"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
