ID<code>argon:web_swing</code> On activation, attaches a rope anchor and swings you like a pendulum while enabled. The rope only cancels motion past its length, turning momentum into an arc. Movement keys steer. Ends on disable, or optionally on ground contact or lost line of sight. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>range</code>DoubleThe maximum distance an anchor can attach to, measured from the eye to the exact hit point.✓/<code>attach_to</code><code>block</code><code>entity</code><code>both</code>Which kind of raycast hit can be attached to: a fixed "block" anchor, a "entity" living entity that becomes a moving anchor followed for the rest of the swing, or "both" (whichever the raycast hits first).✗BOTH<code>beam_renderer</code>IdentifierThe id of the beam renderer used to draw the rope from the user to the anchor point.✓/<code>initial_slack</code>FloatExtra rope length, in blocks, on top of the exact distance when the web attaches. 0 (default) starts the rope as long as the current distance, so attaching never snaps or stalls you. Raise it for a more dramatic catch.✗0.0<code>gravity_multiplier</code>FloatScales gravity's pull while swinging. 1 (default) is normal gravity. Other values adjust vanilla's gravity rather than replace it.✗1.0<code>pump_acceleration</code>FloatAcceleration, blocks/tick^2, from holding forward or back along the rope's tangent plane. It fades out as speed nears max_speed and stops below a minimum speed so you can't hover. 0 is momentum only.✗0.025<code>air_drag</code>FloatExtra multiplier on velocity every tick while swinging, 0 to 1. 1 (default) keeps momentum (vanilla's own air drag is already undone, see drag_compensation).✗1.0<code>hand</code><code>right</code><code>left</code>Which hand the web comes from (drives left/right animation mirroring). Defaults to left if the beam_renderer id ends in "left", otherwise right.✗/<code>auto_tighten</code>BooleanSlowly takes slack out of the rope (never pulling the user, and never below their current distance plus rope_slack_tolerance), so a swing that goes slack gets a usable rope again instead of the web quietly failing.✗true<code>rope_reel_speed</code>FloatHow fast auto_tighten removes slack, blocks/tick.✗0.12<code>minimum_rope_length</code>FloatAuto-tightening never shortens the rope below this length, blocks.✗3.0<code>rope_slack_tolerance</code>FloatHow much slack, blocks, auto_tighten leaves in the rope.✗0.6<code>max_rope_correction</code>FloatThe most, in blocks per tick, the rope may move the user back onto its radius after an overshoot, so a correction is paid off gradually instead of as a snap.✗1.0<code>drag_compensation</code>BooleanUndo vanilla's per-tick air drag (x0.91 horizontal, x0.98 vertical) while swinging in the air, so a swing keeps its momentum. Turn it off only to compare against plain vanilla drag.✗true<code>max_speed</code>FloatCaps the user's total speed, blocks/tick, while swinging. Defaults to 2.6; 0 removes the cap.✗/<code>slack_visual_scale</code>FloatHow far the rope must sag, as a fraction of its length, before the beam looks fully loose. Only beam renderers like argon:segmented_textured use it, and only on the swinging player's client. Everyone else sees a taut web.✗0.5<code>reel</code>Web Swing ReelIf present, holding jump reels the rope in and holding sneak reels it back out (up to the original attach length), both at "speed" blocks/tick, down to "min_length" blocks at the shortest. Leave unset (the default) to disable manual reeling.✗/<code>auto_release</code>Web Swing Auto ReleaseWhich conditions automatically detach the rope: "on_ground" when the user touches the ground, and "on_blocked_line" when a solid block ends up blocking the straight line between the user and the anchor point. Both default to true.✗AutoReleaseSettings[onGround=true, onBlockedLine=true]<code>swing_assist</code>Web Swing AssistTargeting and assist tuning. Targeting is a direct raycast along the aim first (a valid hit always wins); only if that misses, or hits closer than "min_anchor_distance", a small cone of "anchor_cone_degrees" (default 10) is searched, with aim accuracy weighted far above "anchor_height_weight" (default 0.4, the most a high target can gain over an on-aim one). "velocity_blend_speed" (default 0 = off) blends the travel direction into the aim direction. "ground_clearance_strength" (default 0.5) softens downward speed just before grazing the ground. "lateral_steering_strength" (default 0.02) is the left/right equivalent of pump_acceleration. "swing_jump_strength" (default 0 = pure momentum release) is an optional boost applied if jump is held on release. "fall_damage_grace_ticks" (default 15) forgives fall damage for that long after release. "rope_wrap" (default true) lets the rope catch on the nearest obstruction between the anchor and the user.✗SwingAssistSettings[anchorConeDegrees=10.0, minAnchorDistance=3.0, anchorHeightWeight=0.4, velocityBlendSpeed=0.0, groundClearanceStrength=0.5, lateralSteeringStrength=0.02, swingJumpStrength=0.0, fallDamageGraceTicks=15, ropeWrap=true]</p> <p><p><code>reel</code> (Web Swing Reel)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>speed</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)How fast the line reels in.✗/<code>min_length</code>FloatThe shortest the line can get, in blocks.✗/</p> <p><p><code>auto_release</code> (Web Swing Auto Release)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>on_ground</code>BooleanRelease the line when the user lands.✗/<code>on_blocked_line</code>BooleanRelease the line when something blocks it.✗/</p> <p><p><code>swing_assist</code> (Web Swing Assist)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>anchor_cone_degrees</code>Float (0.0 ~ 45.0)How far from the crosshair an anchor can be and still be picked, in degrees.✗10.0<code>min_anchor_distance</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)The closest an anchor can be, in blocks.✗/<code>anchor_height_weight</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)How much higher anchors are preferred.✗/<code>velocity_blend_speed</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)How quickly the swing direction follows the user's movement.✗/<code>ground_clearance_strength</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)How strongly the swing lifts the user away from the ground.✗/<code>lateral_steering_strength</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)How strongly the user can steer sideways while swinging.✗/<code>swing_jump_strength</code>Float (&gt;= 0.0)How strong the jump off the line is.✗/<code>fall_damage_grace_ticks</code>Integer (&gt;= 0)For this many ticks after releasing, fall damage is ignored.✗/<code>rope_wrap</code>BooleanWhether the line wraps around corners.✗/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:web_swing",
  "range": 30,
  "beam_renderer": "example:beam_renderer_id",
  "max_speed": 2.6,
  "reel": {}
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
