ID<code>argon:zoom</code> While enabled, zooms your view to the magnification in "zoom" and eases back out when disabled. It follows "zoom" as it changes, so a data attachment can let scrolling adjust it. Only affects your own view. SettingsExampleIn a power <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>zoom</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe magnification: 1 is normal, 2 is twice the size, 4 four times. A value, so a data attachment can change it while zoomed. Below 1 counts as 1, 100 is the max. With "level_factor" above 1 it is a level instead.✗2.0<code>rate</code>DoubleHow quickly the view closes on the magnification, per second, when zooming and when "zoom" changes. Higher is snappier. 6 covers about 63% of the way in a sixth of a second.✗6.0<code>level_factor</code>Double1 (default) means "zoom" is the magnification. Above 1, "zoom" is a level and the magnification is level_factor raised to it, so every scroll step changes the view by the same proportion.✗1.0<code>scale_sensitivity</code>BooleanWhether turning the camera slows down as the view zooms in, so aiming stays steady (like a spyglass). At 4x the camera turns a quarter as far for the same mouse movement.✗true<code>scale_render_distance</code>BooleanWhether draw distances grow with the zoom so magnified things stay visible: block entities, other entities, sign outlines and name tags. Only already loaded terrain can show.✗true<code>reset_on_disable</code>BooleanWhether turning the zoom off puts the level back to "base_level" (in "level_attachment"), so the next zoom starts from the base instead of wherever it was scrolled to. Needs "level_attachment".✗false<code>level_attachment</code>Data Attachment IDThe number data attachment that holds the zoom level (the one "zoom" reads and scrolling changes), which "reset_on_disable" sets back to "base_level". Only used by "reset_on_disable".✗none<code>base_level</code>IntegerThe value "reset_on_disable" sets the level attachment to.✗0</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:zoom",
  "zoom": 4,
  "rate": 8,
  "reset_on_disable": true,
  "properties": {
    "title": "Zoom"
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "name": "Example Power",
  "icon": "minecraft:command_block",
  "abilities": {
    "zoom": {
      "type": "argon:zoom",
      "zoom": 4,
      "rate": 8,
      "reset_on_disable": true,
      "properties": {
        "title": "Zoom"
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

