ID<code>argon:fade</code> Wraps another render layer and draws it at a changing opacity so it can fade in and out. Put the wrapped layer's conditions inside "layer". Nothing is drawn at opacity 0. SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>opacity</code>Float / Value(Dynamic) 0 to 1, how opaque the wrapped layer is. Usually an ability's eased animation timer, e.g. palladium.get_animation_timer_eased('namespace:power#ability'), which already runs 0 to 1.✗1.0<code>layer</code>Render LayersThe render layer to draw, written exactly as it would be on its own, including its "conditions".✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:fade",
  "opacity": {
    "type": "palladium:molang_float",
    "molang": "palladium.get_animation_timer_eased('example:power#some_ability')"
  },
  "layer": {
    "texture": {
      "type": "palladium:eye_selection",
      "color": "#6b6b6b"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:motion_blur</code> A short, translucent, tapering ribbon built from the entity's recent positions that reads as a motion blur, with optional thin secondary streaks and surface dust. It follows the entity's actual speed: nothing is drawn below minimum_trail_speed, and length, opacity and width grow smoothly towards maximum_trail_speed. Use with tick_delay 1 and a lifetime of at least max_age. SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>texture</code>Texture ReferenceTexture drawn along the ribbon. The first axis runs from the entity to the tail, the second across the ribbon, with the soft centre in the middle.✗argon:textures/trail/motion_blur.png<code>color</code>ColorMain colour of the blur.✗#648aa3<code>highlight_color</code>ColorColour the centre moves towards at high speed.✗#d6e4ea<code>edge_color</code>ColorColour of the faint outer boundary.✗#3b6687<code>opacity</code>FloatOpacity at full intensity, before the speed opacity multiplier.✗0.55<code>trail_start_width</code>FloatRibbon width in blocks next to the entity.✗0.6<code>trail_end_width</code>FloatRibbon width in blocks at the oldest end.✗0.08<code>trail_taper_curve</code>FloatExponent of the taper. 1 is linear, higher keeps the ribbon wide for longer before narrowing.✗1.4<code>trail_height</code>FloatHeight in blocks of the vertical sheet crossing the ribbon. 0 draws only the flat sheet.✗1.4<code>max_age</code>FloatTicks a ribbon segment stays visible at full intensity.✗6.0<code>smoothing</code>FloatHow strongly the ribbon curves between recorded positions. 0 gives straight lines with sharp corners.✗0.4<code>glow</code>BooleanIf true, the ribbon is drawn additively and unaffected by world light.✗false<code>streaks</code>Motion Blur StreaksThin secondary streaks beside the ribbon.✗/<code>speed</code>Motion Blur SpeedHow the effect reacts to the actual movement speed in blocks per second.✗/<code>dust</code>Motion Blur DustBlock particles kicked up from the ground while running.✗/<code>lod</code>Motion Blur DistanceDistance quality: beyond far_distance only a simplified ribbon is drawn, beyond cull_distance nothing.✗/</p> <p><p><code>streaks</code> (Motion Blur Streaks)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>enabled</code>BooleanWhether the streaks are drawn.✗true<code>count</code>Integer (0 ~ 12)How many streaks are drawn.✗3<code>width</code>FloatThe width of a streak in blocks.✗0.08<code>lifetime</code>FloatHow many ticks a streak lasts.✗4.0<code>opacity</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)The opacity of the streaks.✗0.2<code>color</code>ColorThe color of the streaks.✗#a8b8c3</p> <p><p><code>speed</code> (Motion Blur Speed)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>minimum_trail_speed</code>FloatThe speed in blocks per second below which nothing is drawn.✗6.0<code>maximum_trail_speed</code>FloatThe speed in blocks per second at which the effect is at full intensity.✗22.0<code>intensity_curve</code>FloatThe exponent that shapes how intensity grows between the two speeds.✗1.0<code>length_multiplier</code>FloatMultiplies the ribbon length at full intensity.✗1.0<code>opacity_multiplier</code>FloatMultiplies the opacity at full intensity.✗1.0<code>width_multiplier</code>FloatMultiplies the ribbon width at full intensity.✗1.5<code>acceleration_response</code>Float (0.0 ~ 1.0)The share of the intensity gap closed each tick while speeding up.✗0.25<code>deceleration_fade</code>FloatHow many ticks the effect takes to fade out after slowing down.✗4.0</p> <p><p><code>dust</code> (Motion Blur Dust)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>enabled</code>BooleanWhether dust is kicked up from the ground while running.✗true<code>max_per_tick</code>Integer (0 ~ 16)The most dust particles spawned per tick.✗3<code>lifetime</code>Integer (1 ~ 200)How many ticks a dust particle lives.✗10<code>range</code>FloatHow far from the camera dust is still spawned, in blocks.✗32.0<code>turn_burst</code>BooleanWhether sharp turns release an extra burst of dust.✗true<code>splash</code>BooleanWhether dust splashes up when running through water.✗true</p> <p><p><code>lod</code> (Motion Blur Distance)</p></p> <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>far_distance</code>FloatBeyond this distance in blocks only a simplified ribbon is drawn.✗40.0<code>cull_distance</code>FloatBeyond this distance in blocks nothing is drawn.✗96.0</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:motion_blur"
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:ability_bar_slot</code> The slot, counting from 0, that the player has put the given ability in on the given ability bar (in the current preset, normal or crouch), or -1 if it is not assigned. Use it as an ability's list_index so assigned abilities sit together on one page of the ability list in the order of their slots, however many abilities the pool holds. Returns Double SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>ability_bar</code>Ability ReferenceThe argon:ability_bar ability.✓/<code>ability</code>Ability ReferenceThe pooled ability to look up.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:ability_bar_slot",
  "ability_bar": "example:power#bar",
  "ability": "example:power#ability"
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:beam_charge</code> Scales a value by how charged the shot of a charged argon:energy_beam was. Use it in that beam's damage, knockback or lift. Multiplies "value" by "min" at no charge and "max" at full charge. Returns Double SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>value</code>(Dynamic) ValueThe value to scale.✓/<code>min</code>DoubleThe multiplier at the lowest charge.✗1.0<code>max</code>DoubleThe multiplier at full charge.✗1.0</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:beam_charge",
  "value": 10,
  "max": 2
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:flight_speed</code> A flight speed that follows an argon:flight_speed_adjuster dial: "base" plus the dial's value divided by its division_amount. Use it for a flight type's "speed" and "sprint_speed". Just "base" while the ability is off. Returns Double SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>ability</code>Ability ReferenceThe flight speed adjuster ability whose dial to follow.✓/<code>base</code>DoubleThe speed with the dial at zero; the dial's bonus is added to this.✗0.0</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:flight_speed",
  "ability": "example:power#flight_speed_adjuster",
  "base": 1.5
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:item_custom_value</code> A number a Tech Table module wrote onto the item in the given slot with its "argon:custom_value" effect, under the name given there. Uses the fallback if the item has no such value. Returns Double SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>slot</code><code>mainhand</code><code>offhand</code><code>head</code><code>chest</code><code>legs</code><code>feet</code><code>body</code><code>curios:head</code><code>curios:necklace</code>The slot whose item to read, e.g. an armor slot or a curios slot.✓/<code>key</code>StringThe name the value was given in the module's effect.✓/<code>fallback</code>DoubleWhat to use when the item does not have the value.✗0.0</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:item_custom_value",
  "slot": "chest",
  "key": "example:core_power"
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:power_age</code> The age, in days, counted by an argon:time_growth ability: the time the ability has been enabled for the player, as a decimal. 0 if the ability is missing. Returns Double SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>ability</code>Ability ReferenceThe argon:time_growth ability whose age to read.✓/</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:power_age",
  "ability": "example:power#growth"
}
</code></pre>

ID<code>argon:karma_icon</code> The Yin-Yang karma icon, tinted by the viewing player's karma. Hovering it opens a panel with the alignment, progress and the chat title toggle. Karma is private, so it always shows the player's own. SettingsExample <p>KeyTypeDescriptionRequiredFallback<code>properties</code>UI PropertiesShared widget properties like position, size, tooltip and visibility.✗{}</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "argon:karma_icon"
}
</code></pre>
